// Erebus Strait: two against two across a polar sea. Each team holds one coast
// of Antarctica under its ice sheet, a glacier between its two starts floating
// out as an ice shelf; two volcanic islands with flooded calderas lie in the
// strait, tabular bergs aground round them. Nothing grows. A grey, windy day:
// a dark, rough sea, cloud low over the ice, snow showers blowing through.
// Skirmish set-up can override the weather (Stormy for a blizzard) and the
// time of day.
(
    biome: Arctic,
    style: Teams,
    weather: Cloudy,
    tweaks: (rain: 0.6, wind: 22),
    time: Morning,
)
